  "recommended_changes": [
    "Validate then retain / and /show documents only, TTL about 60 seconds, LRU cap about 12, clone documents on insert/read.",
    "Unify cache keys for the exact unfiltered category base path and explicit page 1 path. Do not normalize filtered/paged paths together.",
    "After the initial type-2 discovery request, fetch the five remaining category pages with a maximum concurrency of 3 while preserving all actual filters and order.",
    "Homepage / may be prefetched in the same bounded batch. A prefetch failure must not be represented as an empty successful home-video result.",
    "Use inherited legacy client() so host proxy/DNS/ECH remain effective. Do not require net, Local or new Spider helpers."
  ],
  "cancellation_notes": [
    "Every real Call must remain tracked by destroy(); check interruption/destroyed before starting more calls.",
    "Track home-batch calls separately to cancel only this operation on interruption or failure, without canceling unrelated search/detail requests.",
    "Future.cancel(true) or shutdownNow() alone cannot guarantee prompt cancellation of a blocking synchronous OkHttp socket read; explicitly cancel Calls.",
    "Use lifecycle generation or equivalent lock ordering to prevent completed old operations from repopulating caches after destroy/init.",
    "Always shut down per-operation executor; avoid a permanent unmanaged thread pool."
  ],
  "lazy_filter_loading": "Not compatible with the current old-App contract: SiteApi.setTypes binds filters only from homeContent; categoryContent response does not update the type filter definitions. Returning only the first category filters loses functionality.",
  "limits": "Read-only production analysis. Host first category returned HTTP200 in 0.954s; six category bodies saved. The subsequent homepage read timed out at 30s. The first multi-request timing script did not checkpoint timing before failure, so no invented total timing or concurrency gain is reported."
